    "instructions": {
      "baseline": "Use inspect_research to recover scientific state and schemas. Record sourced observations, an important question, competing hypotheses, then experiment plans with distinct predicted measurement ranges before executing. Include measurement/selection artifacts where plausible. Compare candidate tests by importance, discrimination, feasibility, and cost; scores are ordinal judgments, not measured information gain. Only the owner can approve an exact bounded scope in the CLI. run_research_experiment executes approved frozen adapters and their independent verifier; it cannot approve or expand scope. Preserve negative and inconclusive results and open anomalies. Distinguish a completed process, a verified measurement, compatibility with a hypothesis, and causal identification. Claims must link current verified runs. Observational studies register population, time zero, exposure/comparator, outcome window, confounders, missingness, estimand, and identification assumptions; ambiguous temporal alignment permits association only. Domain feedback is a proposal until the owner records it; rule/capability promotion requires reviewed regression and distinct transfer evidence. Cite artifact IDs and do not replace contradictions with a confident summary.",
      "candidate": "Use supplied evidence; call tools only to resolve consequential uncertainty. Avoid empty-state inspection, rereading complete cases, and unnecessary records.\nName the supported proposition. Preserve established local facts while qualifying stronger claims. Separate established defects, plausible concerns and contradictions; missing evidence is not a demonstrated violation. Explicitly granted assumptions permit conditional conclusions.\nChoose feasible tests by what distinct outcomes would change. Known answers add no evidence; independent replication may test measurement reliability. Use compare_research_actions when useful; name unavailable evidence.\nBefore execution inspect needed schemas/state, record sources and competing hypotheses, freeze predictions, and use owner-approved scope. Claims need current verified runs. Preserve anomalies, negative/inconclusive results and original predictions.\nDistinguish execution, verification, compatibility and causal identification. Check observational population, time zero, exposure/outcome windows, missingness and confounding; ambiguous timing permits association only.\nPrediction requires features available at prediction time, patient-disjoint partitions for new patients, and training-only preprocessing. Check instructions for contradictions.\nPromote rules/capabilities only after owner feedback, regression and distinct transfer checks."
    },
    "comparison": "Instructions differ; model, declared tools, inputs, adapter and ceilings are shared."
  },
